ModelReturned: f{"ResponseMetadata": {"RequestId": "8e5f3fd4-2bca-4b8a-9834-b0010afc26c2", "HTTPStatusCode": 200, "HTTPHeaders": {"date": "Tue, 09 Sep 2025 22:30:21 GMT", "content-type": "application/json", "content-length": "1281", "connection": "keep-alive", "x-amzn-requestid": "8e5f3fd4-2bca-4b8a-9834-b0010afc26c2"}, "RetryAttempts": 0}, "output": {"message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "<thinking>\nThe provisioning failure shows a technical error related to null value handling in the code. The error message indicates a String method call failure due to null \"this.type\". To resolve this:\n\n1. Verify what \"type\" field is missing by checking:\n   - Application sections for required fields that might map to this\n   - Spool configuration differences between Adobe/Payzapp flows\n   - Whether this is a new mandatory field not captured in UI\n\nSince the spool_id is Adobe-specific (59dc...), need to consult Adobe debugging flow documentation. The technical failure suggests a code-level null check missing rather than data issue, but confirming data completeness is still critical.\n\nNext steps:\n- Retrieve Adobe flow debugging steps to identify common provisioning failures\n- Check if all required sections were completed (personalDetails, employmentDetails, etc.)\n- Look for recent code changes affecting provisioning logic\n</thinking>\n\n"}, {"toolUse": {"toolUseId": "tooluse_ESSuinj_T4SgTXji18P_Hw", "name": "get_knowledge", "input": {"name": "debugging_adobe_flow.txt"}}}]}}, "stopReason": "tool_use", "usage": {"inputTokens": 6414, "outputTokens": 221, "totalTokens": 6635}, "metrics": {"latencyMs": 7541}}


