and result
{"text": "# Adobe flow involves 2 stages if cosmos application\n1. DATA_CAPTURE: This is the step where we gather data in Cosmos. Once done, PROVISIONING stage will be initiated\n2. PROVISIONING: This is the stage we do provisoning e.g creating auth profile id, creating/updating account holder, \n    bundle issuance(bundle is nothing but the credit account, cashback account, etc.), card issuance, theme(theme is a physical card color) selection followed by card dispatch\n\n\nturbo-sourcing service takes care of application in DATA_CAPTURE stage.\nturbo-provisioning service takes card of applications in PROVISIONING stage\n\n\n# Here's Sourcing flow,\n1. The external system calls turbo-sourcing services endpoint POST /spools/{spoolId}/applications. This steps will fill the data and creates application\n2. Once application is created, the turbo-sourcing service marks DATA_CAPTURE stage as completed and application will move to PROVISIONING stage by performing complete action. \n\n\n\n# Here's provisoning flow,\n1. When application is in provisioning stage,  kafka invokes turbo-provisioning services \n/spools/{spoolId}/applications/{applicationId}/provisions endpoint. \n2. This endpoint invokes a workflow consisting of steps \n\n- AUTH_PROFILE_CREATION -> This step creats auth profile\n- DEFAULT_CONFIGURATION -> This step adds default configuration for choice of networks(VISA, RUPAY) and default card theme/color \n- VALIDATION -> This step performs dedupe validations, also check if user has existing credit account. If yes, application will be marked as failed with business failure\n- ACCOUNT_HOLDER_SETUP -> This steps updates/creats account holder based on information form cosmso applications sections. mars service APIs are invoked to perform actions \n- BUNDLE_ISSUANCE -> this steps issues credit bundle. aether service's /issueBundle APIs will be involed to perform this\n- CARD_ISSUANCE -> This setps issues selected card networks such as VISA. RUPAY. aether's /issuePrimaryCard service APIs will be involed to perform this\n- CARD_STATUS_VALIDATION -> This steps ensure if issued cards are activate and ready for use. aether's api/v3/tenants/{ifiId}/bundleDetails/{issuanceId} API will be invoked to check the card status\n- THEME_SELECTION - This steps makes a card theme/color selection out off all available themes.\n- DISPATCH -> At the end, this step dispatches the card. -> turbo-account-management-service's /obCompletion  endpoint will be invoked to dispatch the card.\n\n\n\n# ebugging Syteps to be followed.\n1. Get required data from cosmos tables\n2. Fetch logs based on API endpoints. use * format while searching for logs. From the log you can query for mdc.trace_id field which returns the logs of full flow. \ntrictly use regexes as many as possible to not over fetch logs.\n3. Query elastic search index \"service-logs\".\n4. Analyze the field such as parsedMessage.title, parsedMessage.attributes.stackTrace, parsedMessage.attributes.message\nand figure out the possible issue.\n5. You can request for knowledge base for any additional knowledge. \n6. Most probably, query parsedMessage.title with cosmos application wildcard and you will get the the flow id with which you can get the full flow logs\n\n\n\nLog fields description\ntimestamp -> e.g. 2025-09-09T15:10:29.281928105Z\"\napp -> The name of service who pushed this log e.g. \"turbo-provisioning\"\nclusterName -> Kunernetes cluster this service recides in e.g \"turboonboarding\"\nhost -> kubernetes pod id. e.g. \"turbo-provisioning-587fc96bf5-gwg7z\", \nlogger -> Logger e.g. \"in.zeta.springframework.boot.commons.logging.HttpLogger\"\npod -> kubernetes pod id. e.g \"turbo-provisioning-587fc96bf5-gwg7z\"\nlevel ->  log level\ntrace_id -> Trace id common for all the logs in a flow. Can be used to fetch the whole flow logs. e.g. \"67f8ef39325c8465e877893428aa2ca9\"\nspan_id -> distributed tracing span id.\nbaggage#flow_name -> flow name e.g \"turboonboarding.turbo-provisioning--other\"\nbaggage#upstream -> parent service who invoked this call. e.g. \"turbo-provisioning\"\nbaggage#auth_profile_id -> auth_profile_id of the token used to invoke this flow. e.g \"hB5HyA_afplZ5yWQ9o5bNQ==\"\nparsedMessage.title -> Log titles appear here. Its a API path for HttpLogger\nparsedMessage.attributes -> Additional request attributes"}




